WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:13.481
Hey, Little Fox readers.

2
00:00:14.341 --> 00:00:16.102
It's me, Alex, again.

3
00:00:17.022 --> 00:00:22.445
I just got back from ice hockey practice; our coach showed us how to use the neutral zone

4
00:00:22.525 --> 00:00:28.348
trap. That's a strategy to keep the other team trapped in the middle of the hockey rink.

5
00:00:29.224 --> 00:00:34.907
The trap is supposed to stop opposing players from entering our zone and scoring goals.

6
00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:40.070
But I wanted to tell you about another zone we just learned about from Mr.

7
00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:47.654
Fay. It's the Demilitarized Zone, or DMZ, which separates North and South Korea.

8
00:00:48.635 --> 00:00:56.920
Even though it's referred to as a demilitarized zone, the DMZ is the most heavily fortified border in

9
00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:57.500
the world.

10
00:00:59.144 --> 00:01:04.927
You probably already know this, but Korea wasn't always divided into two separate countries.

11
00:01:06.027 --> 00:01:09.248
During World War II, Japan controlled Korea.

12
00:01:10.169 --> 00:01:17.832
When Japan lost the war, the Soviet Union and United States temporarily took control of the peninsula, with

13
00:01:17.892 --> 00:01:21.854
the Soviet Union in the North and the United Sates in the South.

14
00:01:23.154 --> 00:01:32.934
By 1948 two separate countries had been formed—the Democratic People's Republic of Korea (North Korea) and the Republic

15
00:01:32.994 --> 00:01:34.754
of Korea (South Korea).

16
00:01:35.694 --> 00:01:42.976
The two nations were divided along the earth's 38th parallel, or 38 degrees north of the equator.

17
00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:48.038
Each side claimed to be the legitimate government of all of Korea.

18
00:01:49.058 --> 00:01:55.920
Then in 1950 North Korea invaded South Korea, with help from the Soviet Union.

19
00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:02.242
The South fought back, aided by the United States, as well as the United Nations.

20
00:02:03.983 --> 00:02:10.486
Fighting continued for three years, until the two sides finally reached a cease-fire agreement.

21
00:02:11.466 --> 00:02:18.869
The 1953 cease-fire agreement reestablished the border between the two countries near the 38th parallel.

22
00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:25.352
This border became known as the Military Demarcation Line, or MDL.

23
00:02:26.456 --> 00:02:35.739
Both sides pulled back two kilometers from the MDL, leaving a four-kilometer buffer zone—the DMZ—between the two nations.

24
00:02:36.759 --> 00:02:46.602
Today this buffer zone is an extremely dangerous place, with razor wire, watchtowers, heavy artillery, and soldiers lined

25
00:02:46.662 --> 00:02:49.663
up along both its northern and southern boundaries.

26
00:02:50.763 --> 00:02:57.069
Soldiers are allowed to patrol inside the DMZ, but they are not allowed to cross the MDL.

27
00:02:58.029 --> 00:03:03.911
The only place in the DMZ where soldiers from the two Koreas face each other is the Joint

28
00:03:03.971 --> 00:03:06.152
Security Area (JSA).

29
00:03:07.712 --> 00:03:14.614
Built on the village of Panmunjom, the JSA is bisected by the MDL, which is marked with a

30
00:03:14.734 --> 00:03:16.375
low concrete slab.

31
00:03:17.375 --> 00:03:25.061
The JSA contains a small number of buildings, including watchtowers and several low blue buildings owned by the

32
00:03:25.221 --> 00:03:32.904
U.N. Diplomatic talks between North and South Korea are sometimes held in a conference room inside one of

33
00:03:32.964 --> 00:03:33.704
these U.N.

34
00:03:33.744 --> 00:03:41.386
buildings. In order to be stationed in the JSA, a South Korean soldier must hold a black belt

35
00:03:41.546 --> 00:03:45.707
in either taekwondo or judo and be at least 177 cm tall.

36
00:03:48.768 --> 00:03:54.852
The South Korean soldiers guard the area with fists clenched and stony facial expressions.

37
00:03:55.813 --> 00:04:03.338
They also wear mirrored sunglasses, which prevents them from staring directly into the eyes of North Korean troops.

38
00:04:04.319 --> 00:04:07.762
Mr. Fay said that could lead to a dangerous conflict!

39
00:04:09.343 --> 00:04:14.066
North Korea also puts only highly trained soldiers in the JSA.

40
00:04:14.987 --> 00:04:20.794
Like the South Korean soldiers, the North Korean troops assume a rigid military stance.

41
00:04:21.774 --> 00:04:28.037
Despite the cease-fire agreement, a few violent incidents have occurred in the DMZ over the years.

42
00:04:29.137 --> 00:04:37.261
One especially tragic event happened in 1976, when a small group of South Korean and American soldiers were

43
00:04:37.361 --> 00:04:40.523
pruning a tree to improve their view of a checkpoint.

44
00:04:41.583 --> 00:04:49.263
After ordering the troops to stop, North Korean soldiers attacked and murdered two American officers with axes.

45
00:04:50.224 --> 00:04:53.926
To avoid reigniting the war, South Korea and the U.S.

46
00:04:53.986 --> 00:04:57.228
decided not to retaliate with military force.

47
00:04:58.208 --> 00:05:04.652
Instead a large group of soldiers returned to the site three days later and cut the tree down

48
00:05:04.712 --> 00:05:07.353
completely. Mr.

49
00:05:07.413 --> 00:05:12.016
Fay told us that secret tunnels have also been discovered under the DMZ.

50
00:05:13.248 --> 00:05:22.516
In 1974 a South Korean patrol group discovered the first one, which had electricity, lighting, sleeping areas, and

51
00:05:22.616 --> 00:05:24.177
storage areas for weapons.

52
00:05:25.298 --> 00:05:28.201
Since then even more tunnels have been found.

53
00:05:29.102 --> 00:05:36.908
Today the landscape in the DMZ consists of wetlands, forests, mountains, and big open fields.

54
00:05:37.949 --> 00:05:44.657
If it hadn't become the DMZ back in 1953, the land probably would have been developed by now.

55
00:05:45.637 --> 00:05:50.498
But instead the area has become an amazing wildlife sanctuary.

56
00:05:51.479 --> 00:05:59.821
In the DMZ you can see flying squirrels, along with very rare animals like Asiatic black bears and

57
00:05:59.921 --> 00:06:01.061
Chinese gorals.

58
00:06:02.102 --> 00:06:09.924
Two of the most endangered bird species in the world—the white-naped crane and the red-crowned crane—have also been

59
00:06:09.984 --> 00:06:10.664
spotted here.

60
00:06:12.236 --> 00:06:18.699
By now most of the land in South Korea has been developed, and North Korea's landscape has suffered

61
00:06:18.779 --> 00:06:20.580
from severe deforestation.

62
00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:28.383
So environmental groups want to preserve this pristine ecosystem, even if Korea becomes unified again.

63
00:06:29.244 --> 00:06:35.267
The DMZ may be the front line between two countries that are technically still at war, but it

64
00:06:35.327 --> 00:06:38.128
has also become a popular tourist destination.

65
00:06:39.064 --> 00:06:46.591
About 100,000 people visit the JSA each year, with tour guides taking many of them into the U.N.

66
00:06:46.631 --> 00:06:50.034
conference room and even into the secret tunnels.

67
00:06:51.135 --> 00:06:58.502
If you ever travel to the DMZ, you'll need to remember that soldiers across the MDL are watching

68
00:06:58.542 --> 00:07:05.108
you. You can only look in certain directions, and you need permission before taking pictures.

69
00:07:06.684 --> 00:07:12.388
Under no circumstances can you point or wave at anyone on the other side of the border.

70
00:07:13.389 --> 00:07:19.734
Both sides are ready to fight at a moment's notice, so you have to avoid doing anything that

71
00:07:19.754 --> 00:07:20.914
could be misinterpreted!

72
00:07:21.875 --> 00:07:27.519
The DMZ definitely sounds dangerous, but I'd really like to visit it one day.

73
00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:34.909
Mr. Fay described it as one of the most unique and fascinating places in the world—a place where

74
00:07:34.989 --> 00:07:39.052
two countries are divided by a line that cannot be crossed.

75
00:07:39.992 --> 00:07:43.535
Well, Little Fox readers, I'd better get ready for bed now.

76
00:07:44.216 --> 00:07:46.657
My hockey team has a big game tomorrow.

77
00:07:47.618 --> 00:07:52.602
Hey maybe we'll get a chance to use the neutral zone trap—and win the game!
